A record whose frontmatter is not valid YAML gets a `frontmatter` finding on the file line of the
problem, carrying the parser's problem text and its line and column.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
latest_migration: 9999
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/specs/value/0001-first.md --
---
type: value
title: First
summary: The value: one that breaks YAML.
kind: value
created_by: owner
created_at: 2026-01-01
updated_at: 2026-01-01
---

Why the project exists.

## In practice

It shows in every run.
-- cmd --
booping specs check
-- exit --
1
-- stdout --
vault/specs/value/0001-first.md:4  error  frontmatter  mapping values are not allowed here, line 4, column 19
-- stderr --
1 record(s) checked: 1 error(s), 0 warning(s)
